{
  "area": "routine-intents",
  "description": "The two things core says to a host about a routine: where to go and how pressing it is (US-2), and what the body looks like doing it (US-3). Four atoms and an integer — no path, no speed, no clip, no frame. US-2 and US-3 of 125-npc-routines-and-locomotion.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a-shift-about-to-start-is-hurried-and-standing",
      "note": "The ordinary case. Two location atoms and two vocabulary atoms — there is no field on this that could carry a coordinate, and the urgency comes from the goal’s OWN priority rather than a second number authored to say the same thing twice.",
      "input": {
        "actor": "npc_smith",
        "from": "cottage",
        "destination": "forge",
        "priority": 60,
        "tuning": {
          "hurriedAt": 60,
          "urgentAt": 85,
          "idleAt": 0,
          "attemptsBeforeReplan": 2
        },
        "failures": 0,
        "action": "work_forge",
        "authored": {}
      },
      "expected": {
        "intent": {
          "actor": "npc_smith",
          "from": "cottage",
          "destination": "forge",
          "urgency": "hurried",
          "stance": "standing"
        },
        "inPlace": false,
        "urgency": "hurried",
        "replan": false,
        "animation": "idle"
      }
    },
    {
